# Clair's native-window hooks (replace-browser-window design D13). Each hunk
# calls into overlay/chrome/browser/clair/window/, makes Chromium skip UI the
# native window replaces, or switches off a feature Clair removes. The logic
# lives in the overlay; every call does nothing for Chromium's own windows, so a
# bare engine behaves as Chromium.
#
# - browser_window_factory.cc: a normal browser window is ClairBrowserWindow
#   while ClairUI runs (D2).
# - tab_strip_model.cc: a native window adds tabs without a kept position at
#   the top of its sidebar (D12).
# - devtools_window.cc, devtools_window_views.cc: Chromium docks DevTools only
#   through a Views DevtoolsUIController, which a native window doesn't have.
#   These let it dock, and hand the docked DevTools to the card (D5).
# - bubble_anchor_util_views.cc: a native window has no BrowserView to anchor
#   page info and permission prompts to; they attach where it says (D7).
# - toast_controller.cc: ToastController needs a Views anchor and otherwise
#   reaches CHECK_IS_TEST(); a native window shows the toast's text (D8).
# - sad_tab_controller.cc: SadTabController dereferences the BrowserView; a
#   native window shows a crashed page itself (D5).
# - download_ui_controller.cc: a new download goes to the sidebar instead of
#   Chromium's download bubble (D7).
# - browser_web_contents_delegate.cc: Chromium treats every status bubble as a
#   Views one; a native window shows the hovered link's URL itself (D8).
# - browser_prefs.cc, page_visibility.ts: passwords and autofill are off, and
#   their settings section is hidden (D17). In Chromium 156 the section is
#   gated by `yourSavedInfo`; a partial visibility object would hide the other
#   sections' menu items, so every other section is listed as visible.
# - new_tab_page_handler.cc, new_tab_page_feature_promo_helper.cc,
#   extension_install_ui_desktop.cc, read_anything_side_panel_controller.cc:
#   crash sites for a browser without a BrowserView (its footer controller, side
#   panel and toolbar), found by Crest (pauljoda/Crest) on Chromium 156 and in
#   the reading-mode controller's CHECK_IS_TEST(). They skip that UI.
# - settings_clear_browsing_data_handler.cc: clearing history CHECKs for the
#   BrowserView's element to send a promo event; a native window has none, so
#   it skips the event, as Chromium's other users of that element do (D18).
# - constrained_window_views.cc: tab-modal dialogs (JavaScript dialogs, leave
#   prompts, HTTP authentication) are positioned only over a Views host, and
#   browser-modal ones (the extension install prompt) become sheets only on a
#   Views window; a native window is neither, so they'd float in the middle of
#   the screen above every app. They're placed over the card as child windows
#   instead (D9).
# - tab_dialog_manager.cc: tab-scoped dialogs (HTTPS-first's "Ask before
#   HTTP", FedCM's account chooser, autofill and WebUI dialogs) CHECK for the
#   browser's Views widget; in a native window they're parented to its dialog
#   host and placed over the card, as the JavaScript dialogs above (D9).
# - native_widget_mac.mm: a Views widget whose parent view sits in a window
#   no widget owns is a free top-level window; for a native window's
#   permission prompts, page info and dialogs that meant hiding behind the
#   browser window. They're kept as its child windows (D9).
# - render_view_context_menu_mac_cocoa.mm: a page's context menu shows only
#   inside a Views widget; in a native window it shows without one, less the
#   items of D9's unavailable features (adapted from Crest).
# - chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn, components/constrained_window/BUILD.gn,
#   ui/views/BUILD.gn: the overlay's sources.

